Why does everyone thing the luckstone is so useless?

Your luck gets added to your "to hit" roll.  With a luckstone and an
aligned unicorn or altar, you can get your luck up to +10.  Your "to
hit" roll is from 1 to 20.  With that +10 added on, a character at
about level 10 or so (reasonable after completing mines) should
_never_ miss an attack!

Also, your luck deeply affects lots of other things that happen to
you.

When you pray, does your god save your butt or take off a level?

When you drink from a fountain, do you get all your stats increased
(as blessed potion of gain ability), or do you get a bunch of snakes?

When you sit on a throne, do you get a wish or genocide, or do you get
electrocuted?

When you make a wish, do you get what you wanted, or nothing at all?

When you sacrifice, do you get an artifact, or nothing much?

I could be wrong on a couple of these, but luck is _very_ important
for combat, fountains, and praying.

